index ff1a15647..48acfe105 100644
--- a/docs/user/organizer.md
+++ b/docs/user/organizer.md
@@ -53,6 +53,26 @@ Code of Conduct, and Accessibility information before sending people to a live
 registration flow. Policy and legal content remain the operator's
 responsibility.
 
+## Public navigation
+
+Open `/organizer/events/<event-slug>/navigation` to rename, reorder, group,
+hide, or add links in an event's header and footer. The header uses the same
+configured links on desktop and mobile. On sites with a parent-site bar, the
+featured event's navigation also appears on site-level pages.
+
+The default event menu contains Participate, Schedule, Speakers, Sponsors,
+Partners, and Event Info. Past events and Past speakers are not added
+automatically. To add these in the event editor, use full HTTPS URLs with
+**External** enabled: `https://<event-site>/speakers` for the speaker archive,
+or a group linking to `https://<event-site>/events/<past-event-slug>`. Internal
+event links are restricted to the current event. Removing a menu link does
+not remove its page.
+
+With no saved rows, the editor previews the built-in defaults. The first edit
+saves the whole list. Hiding every item keeps the menu empty; deleting every
+saved row restores the defaults. Event identity, search, Help, account controls,
+and the separately managed registration action are outside this link list.
+
 ## Build and publish the program
 
 - Configure the CFP before sending speakers to `/events/<event-slug>/cfp`.
